WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.320
- AMD's RX 6950 XT is almost
a totally different class

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.960
of GPU compared to when it first launched

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.360
to tepid reviews earlier this year.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.130
And with recent price adjustments,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.870
it is such a good deal now

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.570
that its green opponent
no longer makes any sense

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.320
and neither does its
predecessor, the 6900 XT.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.960
But why am I talking
about the 6000 Series?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.960
Because however the RX
7900 Series performs today,

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.500
and it's good,

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.070
I want you to also keep
in mind AMD's track record

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.320
for dramatically improving the performance

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.370
of their GPUs through new
features and driver optimizations.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.470
Personally, I'm counting on it

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.360
because now that I have publicly committed

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.330
to skipping NVIDIA's
latest 40 series cards,

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.453
AMD is my only hope for an
upgrade this generation,

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.700
just like my only hope of paying

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.800
our production team is our sponsor.

